Z||000000||Black88GT||08-04-2000||02:49 PM||||I read on the Fiero OSG that 923 or 912 would be the best to use for brighter tail lights then stock.  I can't find them anywhere.  I did find the 912's but they didn't look like they would fit the socket (I took one with me).  Think a dealer would have them?  I would try another but everywhere I went didn't give MSC or amps or anything on the packaging.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-04-2000||03:15 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.nopi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nopi.com</A>  they carry LED replacements for all the lights in the back.. as well as for the turn signals and super tiny dash lights to come soon. the 1157s and the rest.. they are about $10 each but will never burn out. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||HYPTNOTiSE||08-05-2000||08:12 AM||||Don't buy the LED blubs. I bought them for use in a couple honda accords for "customers".  I got them cheap from Ac1 at a little better than jobbers price. They're not bright.  THey're simply not bright. After buying and installing both sets of bulbs in the hondas, one person came back to me with an inspection ticket cos her taillamps weren't bright enough, and then the cop gave her a ticket for clear lenses. So we had to  revert back to stock, for a few days. The other one, complained, that they simply weren't bright enough, and he wa upset that he paid so much for them per bulb went they dont do what they claim.<BR><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||daved||08-06-2000||11:02 AM||||88GT, I used 918 bulbs on my GT "PON TIAC" lights, though 906 is similar (Thanks to L. Mazza) and this lights up the rear very nicely!<BR>As for the normal tail lights...I think the original brightness is quite adequate.  If you go with higher wattage (brighter) bulbs, there is the danger of socket/taillight meltdown, so use caution, Dave||||reg||1
